<BaseLayout title="Verified AI playbooks" description="Human-reviewed, reusable AI workflows with evidence, limitations, and version history.">
  <div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Verified playbooks</p><h1>Reuse what has been tested, not what merely sounds clever.</h1><p class="lede">A public playbook records a real job, its baseline, the test method, evidence, result, limitations, and review history. Private project details never become public automatically.</p><div class="notice"><strong>The public library is being built from reviewed submissions.</strong> Start a project, complete an evaluation, and prepare a sanitized proof pack from the <a href="/app/">AI Practice Workspace</a>.</div><h2>Publication standard</h2><ol><li>One distinct job to be done and a named audience.</li><li>At least one baseline, one evaluation method, and one limitation.</li><li>No secrets, personal records, unsupported high-stakes claims, or private outputs.</li><li>Human editorial approval, visible version history, and CC BY-SA 4.0 attribution.</li></ol><h2>How the loop compounds</h2><p>Visitors can fork an approved playbook, run it on their own task, report an outcome, and help the next version become more useful. A generated answer is disposable; a reviewed workflow with evidence can improve over time.</p></div>
</BaseLayout>
